1. RECOVERABLE -- how much of the NO tier has an EIN after all 
============================================================================== 
Stratum A (91 cases, simple random from the 845-case NO tier) is the only 
stratum that estimates a rate. It is a simple random draw from 836 of the 
845 NO identities; the 9 held back were held back by an id join later found 
invalid, for reasons unrelated to their content, so the draw stays 
unbiased for the tier. The other 9 cases are labelled B-calibration but 
calibrate nothing -- see section 4 -- and are excluded from every rate.
 
  EIN reported at all        :  31 of 91  34.1% 
    of which WEB-sourced     :  31 
    of which off a candidate :   0 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 
  RECOVERABLE, non-circular  :  30 of 91  33.0%  [24.2%, 43.1%] 
    -> projected over 845 NO : 279 identities [204, 365] 
  RECOVERABLE, incl. candidate-sourced EINs:  30 of 91  33.0%  [24.2%, 43.1%] 
    -> projected over 845 NO : 279 identities 

  The first figure is the headline. The second counts cases whose EIN was 
  read off a rejected near-miss row, which is in the reference BY 
  CONSTRUCTION -- a real recovery route, but not evidence that the 
  reference covers the tier. Both are reported so neither is mistaken for 
  the other. 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 
THE NON-CIRCULAR COVERAGE TEST 
Of the WEB-sourced EINs -- established from a source outside the packet -- 
how many are already in the reference? dev/NO-RESIDUAL-AUDIT.md found 21 of 
21 and called it the robust result, because it is a set-membership test.
 
  A-estimation   30 of 31 in the reference  96.8%  [83.8%, 99.4%] 
  B-calibration  2 of 2 in the reference  100.0%  [34.2%, 100.0%] 
  both strata    32 of 33 in the reference  97.0%  [84.7%, 99.5%] 

  WEB-established EINs that are NOT in the reference -- the only cases 
  that are a reference COVERAGE gap rather than a name-resolution gap: 
    G003195  COMMONWEALTH UNIV OF PENN          ein 232738930  GOVERNMENT 
