4. CALIBRATION -- deliberately NOT done here 
============================================================================== 
The 100-case sample overlaps the prior audit on only a handful of cases, 
and the grant_id join that appeared to give more is invalid -- it pairs 
unrelated grants. See the note in this script and in stage 10 section 3. 
 
The human head-to-head is run separately, on a packet built from the 63 
prior-audit cases that are still NO in this arm: 
  PF_NO_SET=cal Rscript dev/adjudicate-10-no-packet.R 
  PF_NO_SET=cal Rscript dev/adjudicate-11-no-search.R 
  Rscript dev/adjudicate-14-no-calib.R 

(9 truth rows are present in this packet and are IGNORED here.) 
============================================================================== 
5. THE MATCH RATE 
============================================================================== 
The denominators are not interchangeable, so all three are named.
 
  result frame  4,748  identities with >=1 scored candidate. This is the 
                       baseline's denominator and the source of 62.74%. 
  in scope      4,868  every identity the cascade should have resolved, 
                       i.e. all 4,903 less 35 flagged OOS. 120 identities sit 
                       here but not in the result frame: nothing was ever 
                       retrieved for them. 
  all           4,903  every identity in the file. 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 
BASELINE-2026-10C augmented, on its own denominator: 
  4,748 identities, 2,979 YES = 62.74%; 1,044 MAYBE; 725 NO (tier==NO in the result). 
 
The same run on the in-scope denominator, which is the honest one for a 
match rate because it keeps the retrieval failures in: 
  4,868 identities, 2,979 YES = 61.20%  (1.55 points lower) 
  NO tier is 845, not 725: 725 scored-and-rejected plus 120 never scored. 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 
ADDING THE MEASURED RECOVERY (33.0% of the 845-case NO tier, stratum A) 
  recovers ~279 identities.
 
  on the in-scope denominator of 4,868: 
    YES alone                          : 61.20% 
    YES + recovered NO                 : 66.92%  (+5.72 points) 
    YES + cleared MAYBE                : 77.11% 
    YES + cleared MAYBE + recovered NO : 82.83% 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ 
AND ON A CLEANED DENOMINATOR 
Dropping the NO-tier payees that are not organisations the BMF could ever 
hold (56.0% of stratum A), because there is nothing for them to match: 
  removes ~474 identities: 4,868 -> 4394 
    YES alone                          : 67.79%  (+6.59 points, from scope 
                                                   alone, matching nothing) 
    YES + cleared MAYBE + recovered NO : 91.76% 
 
Compare the two levers on the NO tier: recovery is worth 5.72 points and 
the scope correction 6.59. Only one of them is a matching improvement; the 
other is a statement about which grants were ever answerable. 
